# Copy to .env and fill in. Nothing here is required: the site runs without an
# assistant, and the assistant runs without a model (as retrieval only).
#
# Xiona — the support agent.
#
# Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (Google AI Studio).
# Gemini speaks the OpenAI-compatible protocol at the base URL below, so the
# same three variables work for OpenAI, Groq, OpenRouter, Mistral, Cerebras or
# a local Ollama — only AXIA_AGENT_URL and AXIA_AGENT_MODEL change.
#
# LEAVE THE KEY OUT OF GIT. .env is ignored; .env.example is not.
#
# The model name below is the one Google currently lists as stable. Google
# shuts model IDs down on a published schedule — gemini-2.0-flash, the old
# example here, stopped answering on 2026-06-01 — so if the assistant reports
# `model_state: failing`, check the model name before blaming the key:
# https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/deprecations
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#
#   1. cp .env.example .env
#   2. paste your key after AXIA_AGENT_KEY=
#   3. python3 -u server/app.py
#
# .env is git-ignored. The server prints one line at startup saying whether the
# model answered, so you do not have to guess:
#
#   assistant: model OK - it answers. Persian in, Persian out.
#   assistant: model FAILED (provider returned 401). ...
#
# If the model fails, the site keeps working - it answers from its own pages -
# but it answers like a search engine instead of a person.
#
# Model names change. If you see `provider returned 404`, the model ID is gone;
# pick a current one from https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models
# (gemini-2.5-flash is a safe default for a conversational assistant).
AXIA_AGENT_KEY=
AXIA_AGENT_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
AXIA_AGENT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# Seconds before falling back to the retrieved answer.
AXIA_AGENT_TIMEOUT=20
